%% Aether Research - one run, end to end, across every process
%% Source of truth: app/api/v1/research.py, app/workers/*, app/agents/graph.py,
%% app/research/{eventbus,recorder}.py
%% Render: any Mermaid renderer.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor B as Browser
    participant A as API process (FastAPI)
    participant P as PostgreSQL
    participant R as Redis (queue + pub/sub)
    participant W as Worker process
    participant G as LangGraph + 9 agents
    participant X as Gateway / toolbelt / internet

    rect rgb(238, 245, 255)
    Note over B,A: 1. Accepting the work - boundary 2, the public HTTP surface
    B->>A: POST /api/v1/research {question, mode, depth, domains, document_ids}
    A->>A: resolve principal from the opaque session cookie
    A->>R: draw on the token bucket for this identity and route class
    A->>A: validate body (Pydantic), check upload ids belong to the caller
    A->>P: INSERT research_projects (if new) + research_runs status=queued
    A->>P: INSERT audit_log (outside the request transaction)
    A->>R: enqueue {run_id} -- boundary 3, only an id crosses
    A-->>B: 202 Accepted {run_id}
    Note right of A: The API has now finished. It never runs a graph.
    end

    rect rgb(240, 248, 238)
    Note over B,A: 2. Attaching the live feed
    B->>A: GET /research/{id}/events (EventSource, Last-Event-ID if reconnecting)
    A->>P: replay research_events above that seq
    A-->>B: replayed events
    A->>R: SUBSCRIBE run channel
    Note right of A: heartbeat comment every 15 s so intermediaries do not close it
    end

    rect rgb(247, 242, 251)
    Note over W,X: 3. Taking the run - at-least-once, arbitrated by the row
    R->>W: reserve {run_id}
    W->>P: UPDATE research_runs SET worker_id, heartbeat_at WHERE status=queued
    alt no row changed
        P-->>W: 0 rows - another worker already holds it
        W->>W: drop the job, no lock needed (ADR 0017)
    else claimed
        P-->>W: the lease (run + worker_id + attempt)
        W->>P: ingest the run's attached uploads into its corpus
        W->>G: invoke or resume by langgraph_thread_id
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 246, 236)
    Note over W,X: 4. One node, repeated - this block is the whole loop
    loop for every node the graph executes
        G->>G: cancellation check, then the FR-8 gate BEFORE the work
        G->>X: model call by role+mode, or a guarded tool call
        X-->>G: completion or untrusted content, priced and recorded
        G->>P: agent_runs + tool_calls + llm_calls (the only cost tally)
        G->>P: checkpoint the full state (durability=sync)
        G->>W: node finished
        W->>P: UPDATE status, phase, progress, counts - naming its own worker_id
        W->>P: renew heartbeat_at
        W->>P: INSERT research_events (the insert allocates seq, ADR 0018)
        W->>R: PUBLISH to the run channel
        R->>A: event
        A-->>B: data: {...}
    end
    end

    rect rgb(253, 240, 239)
    Note over W,P: 5. What happens when it goes wrong
    alt worker is killed, deployed over, or partitioned away
        W--xW: stops renewing the heartbeat
        Note over P: another worker's sweep sees a stale lease and re-dispatches
        R->>W: reserve again
        W->>G: resume from the last checkpoint, not from the start
        Note right of G: repeated work is harmless - ingestion and writes<br/>are idempotent on content hash and natural key
    else the run hits a hard ceiling
        G->>G: discovery stops; the first reason and a measured caveat are recorded
        G->>G: route straight to the synthesizer - the run still produces a report
    else the user cancels
        B->>A: POST /research/{id}/cancel
        A->>P: UPDATE status = cancelled
        G->>P: reads that column at the next node boundary and stops
    end
    end

    rect rgb(240, 248, 238)
    Note over W,B: 6. Finishing
    G->>G: citation validator walks every marker back to a real source
    W->>P: evidence chain and report in ONE transaction<br/>(the citations' foreign keys require that order)
    W->>P: UPDATE research_runs status=completed, cost, tokens, source_count
    W->>R: PUBLISH report_completed
    R->>A: report_completed
    A-->>B: data: report_completed
    B->>A: GET /research/{id}/report
    A->>P: report + sections + citations, scoped by user_id
    A-->>B: 200 with the citation check's verdict
    end
